! DF on a refill address, the OTHER half of Reference Manual p.32's
! class 3: "the refill address used in INDEX REFILL OPERATIONS".
! df_refill_alarm.strap covers the two operations the same sentence
! names, R and REFILL ON COUNT ZERO; this covers the refills that
! COUNT AND BRANCH and the index-arithmetic operations issue when a
! count reaches zero -- CBR, V+CR, V+ICR and V-ICR.
!
!
! SUPERSEDED 2026-09-24, AND THE CORRECTION MATTERS MORE THAN THE
! PROGRAM.  The "weaker standard" note above rests on the claim that no
! listing here tests DF.  THAT CLAIM IS FALSE.  jb_ax5b routine 1260
! TEST 8C -- PDF pp.76-83, octal 022546.00-022732.40, labels
! I60127-I60146 -- is a dedicated test of the DF AND IF INDICATORS
! under four enable/mask conditions, verified first-hand at 400 dpi:
!
!   I60127 LVI,$X1,I60AD1  -TEST 8C CHECKS DF + IF UNDER 4 CONDS,
!                          -1. DISABL MASK 0 FETCH OK IND NO INT
!                          -2. DIAABL MASK 1 FETCH OK NO IND NO INT
!                          -3. ENABLE MASK 0 FETCH OK IND ON NO INT
!                          -4. ENABLE MASK 1 NO FETCH IND ON INTRPT
!
! Condition 4 is the MASK-DEPENDENT half these programs scope out.  So
! this file was written to a weaker standard than was available, in a
! document this project had already read, thirty pages before the
! routine whose misreading produced the claim.  The program is not
! thereby wrong -- but it is not the strongest evidence available, and
! TEST 8C is the acceptance test it should be checked against.  See
! docs/NEXT.md item 2.
! WEAKER STANDARD, hand-written from p.32, for the reason
! df_data_fetch_alarm.strap states: no listing this project has read
! tests DF at all.
!
! EVERY BLOCK IS PAIRED, count-one against count-five, and the pairing
! is the point.  p.26 says CBR "is identical to COUNT AND BRANCH,
! except that in addition the index word specified by J is refilled if
! the count reached zero", and V+ICR "except that in addition the
! index specified by J is refilled if the count reached zero".  A
! refill that does not happen reads nothing, and p.32's own opening
! sentence is "all storage addresses ACTUALLY USED by the CPU in the
! course of an operation are subject to address monitoring".  So every
! signal below sits inside its own count gate, and the count-five
! block is what makes that a tested claim.
!
! AN OPEN QUESTION THIS TOUCHES AND DOES NOT ANSWER.  The model
! suppresses a refill whose address is 1-15 for R and RCZ only --
! refillLegal, from routine 1238's TEST 2G/2H.  Whether the same
! suppression applies to these refills is NOT stated on pp.25-26,
! which were read for this program and describe R, RCZ, V+ICR, CB and
! CBR without mentioning it; 1238 established it empirically for the
! REFILL operations alone.  The asymmetry in the model is therefore
! untested in either direction and is recorded in docs/NEXT.md rather
! than guessed at here.  It does not affect this program: every refill
! address below is ordinary core, and p.31's carve-out means only an
! address of 32 or more could signal anyway.
!
! MASK-ZERO ONLY, same scope and same reason as its two companions.
!
! Instructions: BD, BE, LVI, SV, LX, KV, CBR, V+CR, V+ICR, V-ICR, BB,
! BB1, BBZ, BZB, B, BEW -- all implemented.

        SLC, (8)4100.0
START   BD,  $+.32
        LVI, $X13, TBL
        SV,  $X13, $IA
        LVI, $X13, RFSRC
        SV,  $X13, $LB               ! lower boundary := RFSRC
        LVI, $X13, ABOVE
        SV,  $X13, $UB               ! upper boundary := ABOVE
        BBZ, 3.57, $+1.0             ! control bit := 0: signal INSIDE
        BBZ, 12.20, $+1.0            ! DF's mask bit := 0
        BE,  $+.32
!
! ---- 1. COUNT, BRANCH AND REFILL, count 1 -> 0 -------------------
!   The count reaches zero, so CBR refills and does NOT branch.
        LX,  $X3,  KC1               ! count 1, refill -> RFSRC
        CBR, $X3,  $                 ! hang if it branched at count zero
        BZB, $DF,  $                 ! hang if the refill address missed DF
        BB,  $IF,  $                 ! hang if it lit bit 21 instead of 20
        BBZ, $DF,  $+1.0
        KV,  $X3,  RFCOPY            ! and the refill LANDED
        BZB, $XE,  $
!
! ---- 2. the same instruction whose count does NOT reach zero -----
        LX,  $X3,  KC5               ! count 5, same refill field
        CBR, $X3,  $+.32             ! branches: count is not zero.  THE
                                     !   TARGET IS THE NEXT HALF-WORD, not
                                     !   the next WORD: CBR is half-word
                                     !   format, so "$+1.0" lands on the
                                     !   SECOND half of the full-word BB
                                     !   below.  Written that way first, it
                                     !   decoded garbage, raised OP, and the
                                     !   machine interrupted into a zero
                                     !   table entry -- and the program still
                                     !   PASSED, because the interruption
                                     !   returned and every later check ran.
        BB,  $DF,  $                 ! hang if a refill that never happened
                                     !   lit DF
!
! ---- 3. ADD TO VALUE, COUNT AND REFILL, count 1 -> 0 -------------
!   ZEROW is OUTSIDE the area, so the operand half-word cannot signal
!   and only the refill address can.
        LX,  $X4,  KC1
        V+CR, $X4, ZEROW
        BZB, $DF,  $                 ! hang if V+CR's refill missed DF
        BBZ, $DF,  $+1.0
!
! ---- 4. and the same with a count that does not reach zero -------
        LX,  $X4,  KC5
        V+CR, $X4, ZEROW
        BB,  $DF,  $
!
! ---- 5. ADD IMMEDIATE TO VALUE, COUNT AND REFILL -----------------
!   The immediate forms read NO operand, so this refill address is the
!   only storage address the instruction uses at all.
        LX,  $X5,  KC1
        V+ICR, $X5, 0
        BZB, $DF,  $
        BBZ, $DF,  $+1.0
!
! ---- 6. and its count gate ---------------------------------------
        LX,  $X5,  KC5
        V+ICR, $X5, 0
        BB,  $DF,  $
!
! ---- 7. SUBTRACT IMMEDIATE FROM VALUE, COUNT AND REFILL ----------
        LX,  $X6,  KC1
        V-ICR, $X6, 0
        BZB, $DF,  $
        BBZ, $DF,  $+1.0
!
! ---- 8. and its count gate ---------------------------------------
        LX,  $X6,  KC5
        V-ICR, $X6, 0
        BB,  $DF,  $
        B,   PASS
PASS    BEW, $
!
! ---- constants, all OUTSIDE the monitored area -------------------
        SLC, (8)4200.0
KC1     XW, 0, 1, RFSRC              ! count 1: the refill fires
KC5     XW, 0, 5, RFSRC              ! count 5: it must not
RFCOPY  XW, (8)123456.76, (8)543210, (8)123456
ZEROW   DD(BU,64,8), 0               ! V+CR's operand half-word
!
! ---- the monitored area ------------------------------------------
        SLC, (8)4300.0
RFSRC   XW, (8)123456.76, (8)543210, (8)123456   ! == the lower boundary
ABOVE   DD(BU,64,8), 0               ! == the upper boundary, first word out
!
! ---- the interruption table --------------------------------------
        SLC, (8)4500.0
TBL     DD, 0
        SLC, (8)4523.0
DSRTN   BB1, 6.0, $+1.0              ! entry 19 = DS
        END, START
